---
/** Features: each part of Clank in turn, with the screen that shows it. */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import SubNav from '../components/SubNav.astro';
import FeatureBlock from '../components/FeatureBlock.astro';
import Window from '../components/Window.astro';
import Crop from '../components/Crop.astro';
import GuideTable from '../components/GuideTable.astro';
import PresetFile from '../components/PresetFile.astro';
import RequestPath from '../components/RequestPath.astro';
import Flows from '../components/Flows.astro';
import FlowsVsOpenCode from '../components/flow/FlowsVsOpenCode.astro';
import Privacy from '../components/Privacy.astro';
import VSCodeWindow from '../components/surfaces/VSCodeWindow.astro';
import BoardShot from '../components/surfaces/BoardShot.astro';
import PhoneShots from '../components/surfaces/PhoneShots.astro';
import { building, context, cost, loopGuard, requests, session, verdict } from '../scripts/crops';
import { LINKS, PAGES, RELEASE, RELEASED } from '../config';
import { phoneFrames, shipped } from '../data/captures';

const sections = [
  { id: 'monitor', label: 'The Monitor' },
  { id: 'context', label: 'Context' },
  { id: 'flows', label: 'Flows' },
  { id: 'flows-vs-opencode', label: 'Flows vs OpenCode' },
  { id: 'gateway', label: 'The gateway' },
  { id: 'models', label: 'Models' },
  { id: 'cloud', label: 'Cloud and cost' },
  { id: 'privacy', label: 'Privacy' },
  { id: 'vscode', label: 'VS Code' },
  { id: 'boards', label: 'Boards' },
  { id: 'phone', label: 'iPhone' },
];
---

<Base title="Features · Clank" description="The Monitor, flows, the gateway, models and engines, cloud cost, privacy, VS Code, boards and the iPhone app: each part of Clank, with the screen that shows it." path={PAGES.features.path}>
  <SubNav slot="subnav" items={sections} label="Features, by section" />
  <PageHeader
    crumb="Features"
    eyebrow="Features"
    title="Every layer between you and the model."
    lead="Each part of Clank in depth, with the screen that shows it: the Monitor and its Guide, the context window, flows, the gateway, models and engines, cloud cost, privacy, VS Code, boards and the iPhone app."
  />
  {
    RELEASE.pending && (
      <p class="container pending">
        The installer installs Clank {RELEASE.latest} today. The live agent panel, boards, artifacts, LaTeX, the agent's
        internet by your allowance and the iPhone app are on Clank's main branch and come with the next release: the{' '}
        <a href={PAGES.changelog.path}>changelog</a> says what each version has.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <FeatureBlock
    id="monitor"
    eyebrow="The Monitor · F10"
    title="Watch a session, and steer it."
    lead="The Monitor follows the folder's newest session: its context window by part, what it does this second, its tool calls, and the Guide to steer it."
  >
    <ul class="points">
      <li><span><b>Live.</b> Its phase, its step, how much it has thought and written, the call it is writing.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>The Guide.</b> Stop, note, pause, compact, undo or drop, each showing its cost before you confirm.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Three views.</b> Flow, Session and Context, one key apart.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <Fragment slot="art">
      <Window title="clank · the Monitor · Session view">
        <Crop crop={session()} label="The Monitor's Session view: the context window by part, what the session does now, and the Guide's keys." />
      </Window>
      <GuideTable />
    </Fragment>
  </FeatureBlock>

  <FeatureBlock
    id="context"
    band
    eyebrow="Context"
    title="Know what fills the window, before it fills."
    lead="The Context view counts each part of the window: the system prompt, tool definitions, thinking, calls and their results, and any text that repeats. It says what you could free, and what that would cost."
  >
    <ul class="points">
      <li><span><b>A margin.</b> Clank tells the agent the window less a margin, so a session compacts before one step's results overflow it.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Beyond the GPU.</b> With KVMem, the exact part is read on the GPU and the rest waits in system memory, so the window can be larger than the GPU holds.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Where figures come from.</b> The engine, the model's template, or an estimate, always labeled.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <Fragment slot="art">
      <Window title="clank · the Monitor · Context view">
        <Crop crop={context()} label="The Context view: each part of the window with its tokens, share and biggest item." />
      </Window>
    </Fragment>
  </FeatureBlock>

  <div class="anchor">
    <Flows />
    <div class="container flow-shots">
      <Window title="Building it with the model">
        <Crop crop={building()} label="Building a flow with the model: the folder read, BRIEF.md written, a draft refused with its problem, then accepted." />
      </Window>
      <Window title="VERIFY's report">
        <Crop crop={verdict()} label="VERIFY's report: a fail with two numbered findings, sent back to PLAN." />
      </Window>
    </div>
  </div>

  <FlowsVsOpenCode />

  <FeatureBlock
    id="gateway"
    band
    eyebrow="The gateway"
    title="One request, end to end."
    lead="Every request the agent makes passes through Clank's gateway, on its way to your GPU or to the cloud. Here is what happens at each hop."
  >
    <ul class="points">
      <li><span><b>Recorded.</b> Each request with its model, its tokens in, cached, out and thinking, and its cost.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Guarded.</b> The loop guard stops an answer that repeats itself while it streams.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Held.</b> Pause a session at the gateway; at a cost limit, cloud requests wait.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <Fragment slot="art">
      <RequestPath />
    </Fragment>
    <div slot="after" class="container gw-shots">
      <Window title="clank · Requests · F7">
        <Crop crop={requests()} label="Requests: one line per request, with its model, tokens and cost." />
      </Window>
      <Window title="clank · the Monitor · live text">
        <Crop crop={loopGuard()} label="The live text of an answer that repeats itself, stopped by the loop guard." />
      </Window>
    </div>
  </FeatureBlock>


  <FeatureBlock
    id="models"
    eyebrow="Models and engines"
    title="Any open model, on the engine you choose."
    lead="A preset says how a model runs: its engine, its file, its window, its most output, its thinking budget. Clank installs llama.cpp (KVMem, for long windows, is built from its source), downloads the model and checks it, asking first at each step."
  >
    <ul class="points">
      <li><span><b>Local.</b> Any open model as a GGUF file, checked by its SHA-256, served by llama.cpp or KVMem.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Cloud.</b> The models OpenRouter offers that take tool calls, with your key.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Switch in one key.</b> Presets are small files: change a number, check it, load it.</span></li>
    </ul>
    {RELEASED && <p><a class="more" href={LINKS.models}>Model setups in the docs</a></p>}
    <Fragment slot="art">
      <PresetFile />
    </Fragment>
  </FeatureBlock>

  <FeatureBlock
    id="cloud"
    band
    eyebrow="Cloud and cost"
    title="Pay per request, and see each one."
    lead="With a cloud model, each request is paid from your OpenRouter credits. Clank shows what each request, session, flow, day and month cost, and pauses at the limits you set."
  >
    <ul class="points">
      <li><span><b>Limits.</b> A day's and a month's, in US dollars; empty means none.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>At a limit.</b> One notice at 80%; at 100% cloud requests wait while local work goes on, until you raise it.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Estimates labeled.</b> A cost is marked as an estimate until OpenRouter gives the exact figure.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <Fragment slot="art">
      <Window title="clank · cloud spending">
        <Crop crop={cost()} label="Cloud spending: today's and this month's against their limits, and this session's cost." />
      </Window>
    </Fragment>
  </FeatureBlock>

  <Privacy />

  <FeatureBlock
    id="vscode"
    band
    wide
    eyebrow="VS Code"
    title="Clank's own VS Code window."
    lead="Your files on the left, OpenCode in a terminal at the right edge, Clank's own view of the conversation beside it, and Clank in the status bar. In review mode, each edit the agent wants opens beside your file with Accept and Reject."
  >
    <ul class="points cols">
      <li><span><b>Review or auto.</b> Review asks before each edit or write of the agent's file tools; auto applies it and opens it after. What the agent's commands change in the folder is not asked about.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>The agent panel.</b> The conversation drawn Clank's way, live: your message shows the instant you press Enter, the model's words as they stream, the header saying what it does; its readout under it: speed, context used.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Completion.</b> Gray text as you type, from a small model on the CPU; Tab takes it.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Figures.</b> Mark up a PNG or JPEG and send it to the agent, each mark said in words.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>LaTeX.</b> Every change the agent makes to a document is built first; a marked-up PDF shows what changed.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Artifacts and jobs.</b> Pages the agent makes from the folder's files, shown and commented on in the editor; long work runs as a job and reports back.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Gates.</b> A flow's gates and questions, answered from the editor.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Elsewhere too.</b> From another computer over SSH, the folder opens in that computer's VS Code, connected to yours.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <Fragment slot="art">
      <div class="surface"><VSCodeWindow /></div>
    </Fragment>
  </FeatureBlock>

  <FeatureBlock
    id="boards"
    wide
    eyebrow="Boards · VS Code"
    title="Lay out a figure with the agent."
    lead="A board is a canvas you and the agent share: a file in the folder. The agent places figures, LaTeX and notes by where they go; you move them, draw on them, pin comments and ask about what you select."
  >
    <ul class="points cols">
      <li><span><b>Figures from the folder.</b> The agent plots the data and places the image; when a script writes it again, the board shows the new one.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>LaTeX on the board.</b> Math drawn at once; TikZ, pgfplots and tables compiled with the folder's TeX, the error shown under the last drawing.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Slots and pins.</b> Draw a slot and press Fill for the agent to make that figure; pin a comment and send the pins. It answers and closes each.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Export.</b> A frame becomes one figure for a paper: PDF for <code>\includegraphics</code>, PNG or SVG. Kept, it is made again each time the frame changes.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <Fragment slot="art">
      <BoardShot />
    </Fragment>
  </FeatureBlock>

  <FeatureBlock
    id="phone"
    wide={!shipped(phoneFrames)}
    eyebrow="iPhone · over your tailnet"
    title="What runs, and what waits for you."
    lead="The iPhone app installs once from a QR code on the console, runs full screen from its own icon, and stays live on one stream from your PC, through your tailnet only: Clank publishes it on your tailnet with Tailscale, never on the internet. It shows the model at work and the machine's load, what waits for you (a change to allow, a question from the agent, a flow's gate), each flow box by box, and a session as the model writes it. Chat, files, notifications and settings come next."
  >
    <Fragment slot="art">
      <PhoneShots />
    </Fragment>
  </FeatureBlock>

  <section class="section next">
    <div class="container next-inner">
      <h2>Ready to try it?</h2>
      <p>Install Clank in one line, then add a cloud key or a model on your GPU.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={PAGES.start.path}>Get started</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .anchor {
    scroll-margin-top: 110px;
  }

  .flow-shots,
  .gw-shots {
    margin-top: 28px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .surface {
    container: surface / inline-size;
  }

  .points.cols {
    display: grid !important;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .soon {
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .next-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .next h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h2);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .next p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-lead);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .flow-shots,
    .gw-shots,
    .points.cols {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>

<style>
  .pending {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    max-width: calc(52rem + 2 * var(--pad));
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .pending a {
    color: var(--blue);
  }
</style>
